Maintainer: Milsurp Monitor Package Signing <bryan@theeverlys.com>
# Deliberately short. A Launchpad builder has no network, so everything the
# build needs is either here or inside the source package -- see debian/rules
# and the `vendor/wheels` tree it installs from.
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 python3 (>= 3.14),
# python3-venv is in universe, which a Launchpad PPA builder has and a
# main-only chroot does not -- see scripts/build-deb.sh, which creates the
# local sbuild image with universe enabled so the two agree.
#
# It pulls in python3-pip-whl, the bundled wheel that `python3 -m venv` uses to
# put pip *inside* the venv. The system python3-pip is deliberately not a
# build dependency: nothing here uses it, and the venv's own pip is what
# installs the vendored wheels.
 python3-venv,
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/bceverly/milsurp
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: milsurp
# Not "all": the vendored wheels include compiled extensions (Pillow, lxml,
# psycopg, argon2-cffi), so the package is tied to an architecture.
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.14),
# Named explicitly because dh_shlibdeps is excluded from the venv (see
# debian/rules), so the compiled extensions in the vendored wheels contribute
# nothing to ${shlibs:Depends}. python3 pulls libc6 in anyway; stating it means
# the package declares what it actually links against rather than relying on
# that.
 libc6,
 adduser,
 nginx,
 sqlite3,
Recommends:
# The OCR binding in the venv is only the Python half. Hunter's Lodge publishes
# a scanned flyer instead of a catalog and its scraper checks for this before
# using it, so a machine without it runs everything else normally.
 tesseract-ocr,
# Selenium drives a real browser for the handful of vendors whose catalog is
# drawn client-side.
 chromium-browser | google-chrome-stable,
Suggests:
 certbot,
 python3-certbot-nginx,
 postgresql-client,
Description: Military surplus firearm listing and price tracker
 Milsurp Monitor scans military-surplus firearm dealers on a schedule, stores
 what they list and tracks how the prices move, so a collector can watch a
 market that is spread across dozens of small shops with no common catalog.
 .
 It reads each vendor's own storefront -- WooCommerce, Shopify, BigCommerce,
 Magento and several one-off platforms -- and normalises what it finds against
 a curated armory of models, manufacturers and cartridges, so that ".32 ACP"
 and "7.65mm Browning" are one filter rather than two.
 .
 This package installs the application into /opt/milsurp with its own Python
 environment, registers a systemd service and ships an nginx site template.
 Configuration lives in /etc/milsurp/config.yaml, which is created on first
 install with generated secrets and never overwritten afterwards.
